; Host-level config consumed by the 'ema' CLI (the DB layer).
;
; One [default] section per host. Unlike reuter.ini (one [<dbname>] section per
; database), this file is host-wide: every instance ema provisions on this host
; reads it, and the value is written into that instance's [mysqld] when the
; instance is provisioned.
;
; ssl-ca is the CA the instance's server verifies CLIENT certificates against —
; the server half of simox's `require: 'X509'` service account. Its value is an
; absolute path on this host; the operator installs the CA there out of band,
; and ema records the path only, never the certificate bytes. Unset (or no file
; at all) emits no ssl-ca line, leaving the instance on plain TCP. EMA_SSL_CA
; overrides the key.
;
; The committed path is simox's convention for the server CA. The real file is
; private data: it lives in simox's private config repo and is materialized into
; etc/ as a real file by bin/fetch-private-data (see
; doc/system/private-config.md). A host that provisions instances (simo0/simo1)
; needs it, and it must be named in DEPLOY_PRIVATE_FILES — the deploy swaps the
; repo directory, which wipes etc/.

[default]
ssl-ca = /etc/simox/ssl/ca.crt
